{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571896458,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MTE3MjI1NTA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3829","origin":"github"},"title":"Supoptimal handling of alternative clone URLs in clone() and calling code","message":"Just documenting my thoughts after seeing this in the context of https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827\n\nWhen `clone()` is called from `get()` is receives a list of alternative URL that are partially generated by `_get_flexible_source_candidates()`. However, `clone()` itself will call this function for any URL it receives. That seems pointless.\n\nMoreover, `clone()` treats the primary source URL different from alternatives. For example, it checks if it is identical to the destination path and stops processing in this case. I am not confident that this distinction is properly acknowledge in all calling code. Maybe it would be better to RF `clone()` to not make this distinction anymore, and have `source=` accepts multiple values, and dissolve the `alt_sources=` argument.","files":null}]}